{
 "about": "Market hours (bullets, dated, 2.38): when each market on the Live page trades, in its own time zone, so a card can say Open / Closed / Lunch break and a price that stopped moving is not mistaken for a live one. sessions: name -> {tz, days (0 = Monday), open / close (HH:MM, local; close before open = runs past midnight), breaks [[from, to]], always (trades all the time), weekly [day, time, day, time] (opens on one weekday, closes on another: futures and currencies), holidays (a rules file with dated holidays)}. tickers: Yahoo ticker -> session; the rest of a group follows its group's session. stale_min: a market that should be open but has had no new price for this long shows 'no update' (a holiday this file does not know). Times change rarely; when one does, add a new session with a valid_from date instead of editing the old one.",
